  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its first run: 13 witnesses pass and the rule uses 27 names. I didn't change anything after that run.\n\nBefore that run, I tried one extra shell command by mistake: the gate command with `--help` piped to `head`. It was blocked automatically, never ran, and doesn't count against the gate budget. I've noted it in `task_result.md`.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_457_1.lean`):\n- **Who it applies to:** a vehicle (`DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`) at rest (`drv_motion_complete_halt`), on a highway it occupies where a lane on that highway has a side marked as a curb.\n- **When it doesn't apply:** the stop is a stop in traffic. That means either:\n  - the lane it occupies is governed by a traffic signal, stop sign, yield sign, railway signal or gate, or a person directing traffic; or\n  - another road user is ahead of it in its lane within `p.queue_halt_gap`.\n- **What it requires:** the obligation picks out the same curbed highway again, then requires one of three things:\n  - **Right curb:** heading parallel to the lane within `p.parked_heading_cos`, with a road edge on the vehicle's right within 18 inches (`Units.inches 18`).\n  - **Left curb:** the left-curb parking permission is declared, the vehicle is on a one-way roadway, parallel the same way, with a road edge on its left within 18 inches.\n  - **Angle parking:** the lane has an angle-parking sign whose conditions hold, or the vehicle is in a parking bay whose angle is more than `p.parking_space_angle_resolution`.\n\n**Choices the node left open** (no narrowings declared):\n- A curb on either side of a lane counts, and the marking's colour isn't restricted, because the text gives none.\n- The bay angle is compared as an absolute value, since the node says the angle must \"stand clear of zero\". This reads wider than the record, not narrower.\n\n**Witnesses:** all 8 planned scenarios are built with their planned verdicts. I added five more so that every part of the rule has a test that changes the verdict:\n- `branch_5` to `branch_8` (not applicable): a stop in a lane governed by a stop sign, a yield sign, a railway gate and a flagger.\n- `branch_9` (compliant): an angle-parking sign with no conditions on its legend.\n\nFiles are in `library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/`:\n- NRS_484B_457_1.lean\n\nFiles are in `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/NRS_484B_457_1/`:\n- task_result.md",
